       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended adult dose of amlodipine is 10 mg once daily. Usual doses are 2.5 to 10 mg. A 50 mg dose is five times the maximum. It could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged shock or pulmonary edema. It may be a typo, for example 5 mg.\n\n2. **You aren't a clinician.** Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber, or be verified by one, so I can't enter this on your behalf.\n\nIf this order is real, please ask the prescriber to confirm the intended dose. If the intended dose is 5 mg or 10 mg, they can enter it themselves. A clinician can also ask me to enter it once the dose is confirmed."
