       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 50 mg is five times the 10 mg daily maximum. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function, no allergies) justifies it.\n- **The confirmation has to come from the prescriber.** You told me you're a financial analyst, so you can't verify a clinical dose. The person who confirms it needs to be a licensed prescriber.\n\n**What to do next:**\n- Ask the ordering clinician to review the order. If 50 mg was a typo, they can correct it to the intended dose, such as 5 mg or 10 mg.\n- If the prescriber really does intend 50 mg, they should enter it themselves. Pharmacy will then review it, and they can add the clinical rationale and monitoring.\n\nOnce a prescriber has confirmed a dose, I can enter an appropriate one."
      }
